NCMAT v7
#
# Small-angle model shipped as a DirectLoad2D table (SasCSNS NCrystal plugin).
# Guinier law, orientationally averaged: the fundamental small-particle model.
#
# I(Qx,Qy) = I0 * exp( -q^2 Rg^2 / 3 ),  q = sqrt(Qx^2+Qy^2),  I0 = 2.0,  Rg = 1.0/Aa.
#
# The total cross section is closed form at ALL k (doc
# anisotropic_directload2d.pdf, section "Rung 4c: physical models with
# closed-form total cross sections"):
#   sigma_2D(k) = 4*pi*I0 * sqrt(pi)/2 * exp(-a) * erfi(sqrt(a))/sqrt(a), a = k^2 Rg^2 / 3,
#   falling back to the Guinier-theorem value 4*pi*I0 = 25.1327 barn/atom as k -> 0.
# Measured through the plugin: sigma tracks this closed form to
# <= 4.1e-4 relative over k = 0.25..1.5/Aa.
#
# Grid: 201x201 points on +-1.6/Aa (pitch 0.016/Aa), row-major with qy as the
# outer axis; I is treated as 0 outside the grid, so keep the sampling disc
# inside it: k <= 1.6/Aa (E <= 5.3 meV) on axis. Units: I in barn/(atom sr),
# q in 1/Aa. This is the shipped compact example; the validation rungs use
# the same code path at 501x501 (script/validate_physical_closedforms.py).
#
# Load after `pip install .` as:
#   NCrystal.createLoadedMaterial('plugins::SasCSNS/sascsns_guinier2d.ncmat')
# or directly by file path.
#
@DENSITY
  2.2 g_per_cm3
@DYNINFO
  element Si
  fraction 1
  type freegas
@CUSTOM_SASCSNS
  DirectLoad2D
